<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch08-the-integral-as-accumulation">
  <title>The Integral as Accumulation</title>
  <shorttitle>The Integral</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>An integral measures an accumulated quantity. Velocity determines displacement, power determines energy use, and density determines mass. We will approximate each total by dividing an interval into small pieces and adding their contributions, then define the definite integral as a limit of these sums.</p></introduction>

